<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech SPT Telecom CZK 6.009 bln 9mo gross.</title>
<headline>Czech SPT Telecom CZK 6.009 bln 9mo gross.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited results for nine-month period ending September 30, 1996, according to International Accounting Standards (IAS), compared with half year 1996, and full-year 1995 results (interim IAS results for 1995 not available) (in CZK millions):</p>
<p>				Jan-Sept 96   H1 1996	FY 1995</p>
<p> profit before tax	   6,009	  4,479	  7,016</p>
<p> income tax expense	 -2,234	 -1,661	 -2,187</p>
<p> profit after tax	    3,775	  2,818	  4,829</p>
<p> revenue			23,276	 15,097	 26,417</p>
<p> operating costs	   -12,725	 -8,199	-13,868</p>
<p> EBITDA			 10,551	  6,898	 12,549</p>
<p> depreciation		 -4,494	 -2,938	- 4,670</p>
<p>net interest and other</p>
<p>     financial charges	 373	    787	  - 876</p>
<p> other			    -421	   -268	     13</p>
<p>ASSETS</p>
<p>tangible assets	     74,653	 67,479	 58,957</p>
<p> intangible assets	     363	    353	   376</p>
<p> investments			 1	     29	    25</p>
<p> fixed assets		 75,017	 67,861	59,358</p>
<p> inventories		   1,726	  1,459	 1,286</p>
<p> receivables		   8,340	 10,551	10,945</p>
<p> cash &amp; cash equivalent   19,531	 22,116	31,578</p>
<p> CURRENT ASSETS	     29,597	 34,126	43,809</p>
<p> TOTAL ASSETS		104,614	101,987     103,167</p>
<p>EQUITY &amp; LIABILITIES</p>
<p> share capital		32,209	 32,209	32,209</p>
<p> reserves		     51,184	 50,323	47,325</p>
<p>SHARE CAPITAL AND</p>
<p> RESERVES			8,340	 82,532	79,534</p>
<p> loans and overdrafts     12,215	 11,707	14,701</p>
<p> creditors		     4,447	  3,312	 4,523</p>
<p>finance lease</p>
<p> obligations		     203	    221	   538</p>
<p> provisions		    4,356	  4,215	 3,871</p>
<p> LIABILITIES		  21,221	 19,455	23,633</p>
<p>TOTAL EQUITY</p>
<p> &amp; LIABILITIES	     104,614	101,987     103,167</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is SPT Telecom a.s., the main Czech telephone operator. The company is 27 percent owned by a Swiss-Dutch consortium comprised of PTT Netherlands and Swiss Telecom.</p>
<p>SPT said that consistent with the 1995 full-year results, the interim numbers include the 51 percent consolidation of EuroTel sro on a line by line basis. The company did not release interim 1995 IAS results.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
